                                                "sense_id": "0b9ce796-faf0-3abb-8950-e16c20e29346",
                                                "text": "Tuvalu, a string of islands northwest of Australia, sold the rights to its suffix, “.tv,” to a Canadian entrepreneur for $50 million, and used the money to put electricity on the outer islands, create scholarships and finance the process to join the United Nations."
